{
  "description": "The import of a fork Config file whose access list a Policy carries as it stands (SDN-27, #203): the Virtual Hub EXACT of tests/golden/configimport/exact.config is the VRF exact with one Network, its users are Users whose groups are the tags of their Nodes, and its access list is the Policies of exact in the order of the fork. Each packet gets the verdict that the fork gives the frame, and none is narrower: a pass entry before a discard entry of one priority, a group and a user of one name, a source address, the ports of TCP and of UDP, a range of ports that a pass entry holds and a discard entry of one port that comes after it, an ICMP entry with a destination, and what no entry matches. The test TestForkImportJudgesEveryFrameAsTheForkDid of controller/internal/explain holds the import to the access list of the fork for every frame of these kinds between every two Nodes; the scenario forkimport has the frames that the fork was run on, and three that the import carries more narrowly.",
  "nodes": {"u1": 1, "u2": 33, "u3": 65, "u4": 97, "blue": 129},
